  "security_implications": "The clearing PRNG provides pseudo-random data used to overwrite key and state registers, preventing secret data retention. Any failure in its handshake, entropy supply, or width mismatch could result in incomplete clearing, leaving key material or sensitive state exposed. The parameter SecMasking disables masking when set to 0, which reduces side-channel resistance and could be a security risk in masked implementations.",
